                "event": "Winter Weather Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 13 at 5:04AM AKST until November 13 at 11:00PM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Snow and mixed precipitation. Total snow accumulations from\n2 to 10 inches.\n\n* WHERE...Kodiak Island Northeast.\n\n* WHEN...Until 11 PM AKST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy snow and rain on snow may create difficult travel\nconditions.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A compact storm will move southeast of Kodiak\nIsland and remain nearly stationary through Friday afternoon to\nevening. Slight deviations in the storm position to the east and\nwest will cause snow levels to fluctuate between sea level and 400\nft in elevation. Kodiak city and the archipeligo to the north are\nmost likely to mix with rain at times, resulting in total snow\naccumulations of 2 to 4 inches. If rain does not mix in, expect\nhigher snow totals. Areas from Kodiak Airport to Women's Bay are\nmore likely to maintain a northwest wind, resulting in colder\ntemperatures, a lower likelihood of rain, and snow accumulations\nfrom 6 to 10 inches.",
                "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. For the latest road\nconditions call 5 1 1 or visit 511.alaska.gov.",
                "response": "Execute",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "WSWAER"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WWAK41 PAFC 131404"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "WINTER WEATHER ADVISORY NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 PM AKST THIS EVENING"
